1
00:00:14,326 --> 00:00:15,156
Mariah Mariah Mariah

2
00:00:15,239 --> 00:00:16,297
Mariah Mariah Mariah

3
00:00:16,380 --> 00:00:23,380
Mor

4
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:48,800
that hurt huh what happened
and what's that bag doing there

5
00:00:53,540 --> 00:00:56,980
no it can't be you mean that bag had a

6
00:01:01,040 --> 00:01:01,870
Ah!

7
00:01:01,953 --> 00:01:02,783
Oh, my God!

8
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:04,980
I ran over a cat! But how?

9
00:01:05,260 --> 00:01:06,937
I didn't even see it lying there!

10
00:01:07,020 --> 00:01:09,917
There was no way I could have
dodged the poor thing in time!

11
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:11,340
Exactly right! Huh?

12
00:01:11,620 --> 00:01:13,502
That was just a bit of bad luck.

13
00:01:13,840 --> 00:01:16,134
It's not like you meant to run it over.

14
00:01:16,540 --> 00:01:18,840
Nah, if you want my take on the matter?

15
00:01:19,040 --> 00:01:21,117
The real scoundrel here is the asswipe!

16
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:23,637
who left that poor kitten in a bag to die.

17
00:01:23,720 --> 00:01:25,700
Pretty rotten, if you ask me.

18
00:01:27,120 --> 00:01:28,557
We've got to do something!

19
00:01:28,640 --> 00:01:30,060
Would it be the point?

20
00:01:30,360 --> 00:01:33,420
You don't hear the little
furball meowing, do you?

21
00:01:33,880 --> 00:01:34,720
It's dead.

22
00:01:35,440 --> 00:01:36,940
So what's your name, kid?

23
00:01:37,360 --> 00:01:38,860
I'm Tamami Kobayashi,

24
00:01:39,140 --> 00:01:43,497
and I just happened to have graduated
from the same school you're attending.

25
00:01:43,580 --> 00:01:45,240
Nice bike you got there.

26
00:01:45,600 --> 00:01:47,140
So are you a freshman?

27
00:01:47,880 --> 00:01:48,710
Yes, I am.

28
00:01:49,120 --> 00:01:50,900
My name is Koichi Hirose.

29
00:01:51,620 --> 00:01:52,960
Ah, high school.

30
00:01:53,340 --> 00:01:55,100
Boy, that sure takes me back.

31
00:01:55,440 --> 00:01:56,297
Good times.

32
00:01:56,380 --> 00:02:00,420
At any rate, have a seat
over here, Mr. Hirose.

33
00:02:01,040 --> 00:02:02,380
Uh... but... but I...

34
00:02:03,940 --> 00:02:05,020
Come on, kid!

35
00:02:05,220 --> 00:02:07,691
Quit that punk-ass quivering and sit down!

36
00:02:08,480 --> 00:02:12,380
Now that you're nice and comfy,
I have a proposition for you.

37
00:02:12,740 --> 00:02:17,220
I'll lay that pussycat to rest, and
you grease my palm with some cash.

38
00:02:17,460 --> 00:02:18,300
Sound fair?

39
00:02:19,160 --> 00:02:19,990
Hey!

40
00:02:20,073 --> 00:02:21,757
There's something wrong with your ears!

41
00:02:21,840 --> 00:02:23,177
What are you talking about?

42
00:02:23,260 --> 00:02:24,142
Try to keep up!

43
00:02:24,280 --> 00:02:25,457
This is serious business!

44
00:02:25,540 --> 00:02:27,420
I know you're innocent and all,

45
00:02:27,540 --> 00:02:32,011
but you're not planning to pull a
hit-and-run with my precious cat, are you?

46
00:02:32,120 --> 00:02:33,857
You're saying that cat belonged to you?

47
00:02:33,940 --> 00:02:35,737
That's exactly what I'm saying.

48
00:02:35,820 --> 00:02:37,777
Then aren't you the one who stuffed the

49
00:02:37,860 --> 00:02:39,917
kitten inside a bag and
left it in the street?

50
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:42,176
Let's not get bogged down in details.

51
00:02:42,280 --> 00:02:45,717
I'm asking if you think you're
gonna walk away from this scot-free.

52
00:02:45,800 --> 00:02:49,760
After all, the killer
here is you, short stuff!

53
00:03:04,160 --> 00:03:06,960
Let's go.

54
00:04:07,980 --> 00:04:10,820
I bet you're feeling
pretty guilty right now,

55
00:04:10,980 --> 00:04:14,037
but the good news is paying
a little fee could just

56
00:04:14,120 --> 00:04:16,797
free yourself of that
oppressive feeling of guilt.

57
00:04:16,880 --> 00:04:21,260
So why don't we begin the healing
by emptying out your wallet? Well?

58
00:04:27,620 --> 00:04:28,450
Ah!

59
00:04:28,533 --> 00:04:29,558
What is this thing?

60
00:04:29,680 --> 00:04:32,151
It looks like some kind of freaky padlock!

61
00:04:32,480 --> 00:04:34,800
And it's really heavy! Huh?

62
00:04:35,040 --> 00:04:36,977
You're saying you could actually see it?

63
00:04:37,060 --> 00:04:37,890
Ha!

64
00:04:37,973 --> 00:04:39,000
What do you know?

65
00:04:39,220 --> 00:04:41,900
That'll make things go
by a whole lot faster!

66
00:04:42,340 --> 00:04:44,516
Wait, you mean this thing is a stand?

67
00:04:44,740 --> 00:04:47,446
Why is a psycho stand
growing out of my body?!

68
00:04:50,280 --> 00:04:51,110
Ah.

69
00:04:51,193 --> 00:04:53,457
Hey Josuke, you seeing what I'm seeing?

70
00:04:53,540 --> 00:04:55,540
It looks like Koichi's down there.

71
00:04:55,720 --> 00:04:57,620
Yeah, that's Koichi, all right.

72
00:04:57,820 --> 00:04:58,879
No doubt about it.

73
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:03,235
No matter where he goes, he always
seems to end up with the wrong crowd.

74
00:05:03,340 --> 00:05:05,164
I'm sure he can handle himself.

75
00:05:05,860 --> 00:05:10,157
Four months ago, I crossed paths with
a guy by the name of Keicho Nijimura,

76
00:05:10,240 --> 00:05:12,946
and he gave me a pretty
handy special ability.

77
00:05:13,160 --> 00:05:16,057
I hadn't a clue what was
happening, but it felt great.

78
00:05:16,140 --> 00:05:18,657
And I figured if I put my
new powers to good use,

79
00:05:18,740 --> 00:05:22,237
I'd never have to worry about a
thing for the rest of my life.

80
00:05:22,320 --> 00:05:24,085
All right, cuff it up already.

81
00:05:24,200 --> 00:05:26,917
Being cheap means the lock
stays right where it is.

82
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:28,697
And you wouldn't want that, would you?

83
00:05:28,780 --> 00:05:30,980
I can't help you, really.

84
00:05:31,440 --> 00:05:32,500
I'm flat broke.

85
00:05:34,200 --> 00:05:36,477
Ah, then explain why you just looked away.

86
00:05:36,560 --> 00:05:38,400
I didn't. I mean...

87
00:05:40,360 --> 00:05:41,720
It got heavier!

88
00:05:42,200 --> 00:05:43,700
Oh, no, I'm gonna...

89
00:05:45,180 --> 00:05:46,580
Tsk, tsk, tsk.

90
00:05:46,820 --> 00:05:49,820
Didn't anybody ever teach
you that it's bad to lie?

91
00:05:50,020 --> 00:05:52,857
Admit it or not, you know in
your heart that I'm right.

92
00:05:52,940 --> 00:05:57,058
And the guiltier you feel, the bigger
and heavier that lock will grow.

93
00:05:57,300 --> 00:06:00,237
The lock's size is proportional
to the weight of your guilt,

94
00:06:00,320 --> 00:06:02,197
and the two are inexorably linked.

95
00:06:02,280 --> 00:06:05,137
You can knock me out or
run a thousand miles away,

96
00:06:05,220 --> 00:06:07,477
but you're never getting
rid of that thing.

97
00:06:07,560 --> 00:06:10,397
So why don't you be a good
boy and give me your wallet?

98
00:06:10,480 --> 00:06:11,310
How about it?

99
00:06:12,400 --> 00:06:15,337
Didn't you say something
about being flat broke, kiddo?

100
00:06:15,420 --> 00:06:17,577
This looks like 7,000 yen to me.

101
00:06:17,660 --> 00:06:18,937
No, you can't!

102
00:06:19,020 --> 00:06:22,417
That's the money I was going to use to
buy new sneakers for gym class today!

103
00:06:22,500 --> 00:06:23,680
Whoa, sneakers?

104
00:06:25,280 --> 00:06:26,860
You could go barefoot!

105
00:06:27,660 --> 00:06:28,490
Hey, man.

106
00:06:28,980 --> 00:06:30,660
What's going on? Huh?

107
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:35,040
Josuke and Okuyasu, you're here!

108
00:06:35,560 --> 00:06:38,560
Looks like a grown man's
mugging a high school kid.

109
00:06:38,740 --> 00:06:41,517
Why don't you get a job
and earn your own money?

110
00:06:41,600 --> 00:06:42,680
Oh, butt out!

111
00:06:42,880 --> 00:06:45,057
It's none of your business, so run along!

112
00:06:45,140 --> 00:06:46,964
Sorry, that's not gonna happen.

113
00:06:47,280 --> 00:06:51,057
Not when there's a stinking shitbag in
his dirty little stand in front of me.

114
00:06:51,140 --> 00:06:53,493
I think it's time to take out the trash.

115
00:06:54,020 --> 00:06:54,850
Hey, now!

116
00:06:54,933 --> 00:06:56,397
Damn thing won't come off!

117
00:06:56,480 --> 00:06:58,068
What kind of stand is this?

118
00:06:58,780 --> 00:06:59,740
Hold on a sec.

119
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:01,588
You guys could see it, too?

120
00:07:01,740 --> 00:07:03,857
How many of you freak shows are there?

121
00:07:03,940 --> 00:07:08,417
You took the words right out of my mouth,
but the answer to that question can wait.

122
00:07:08,500 --> 00:07:11,735
Till then, I'd appreciate it
if you'd remove that lock.

123
00:07:12,520 --> 00:07:13,860
Hey, you assholes!

124
00:07:14,100 --> 00:07:15,737
Don't you underestimate me!

125
00:07:15,820 --> 00:07:18,977
Watch yourselves, because
I'm not fooling around here.

126
00:07:19,060 --> 00:07:21,557
It's essential that criminals
pay for their crimes

127
00:07:21,640 --> 00:07:25,020
in order to keep society
from crumbling around us.

128
00:07:25,420 --> 00:07:29,537
If he's not going to pay, does that mean
one of you will cover what he owes me?

129
00:07:29,620 --> 00:07:31,440
If so, I'll let you go.

130
00:07:32,860 --> 00:07:34,880
Money's money, after all. Oh.

131
00:07:35,940 --> 00:07:38,117
So you just want to get
your hands on our money.

132
00:07:38,200 --> 00:07:39,477
I'd like to see you try.

133
00:07:39,560 --> 00:07:40,497
Keep your guard up.

134
00:07:40,580 --> 00:07:43,157
This loser already
swiped 7,000 yen from me.

135
00:07:43,240 --> 00:07:46,416
That's because you lied
straight to my face, you dolt!

136
00:07:46,500 --> 00:07:51,340
You really think that poor kitty's
life is only worth a measly 7,000 yen?

137
00:07:51,720 --> 00:07:52,820
Well, think again.

138
00:07:53,280 --> 00:07:55,560
You owe me 500 grand, kiddo!

139
00:07:55,720 --> 00:07:56,940
500 grand?!

140
00:07:57,540 --> 00:07:59,860
You bet your ass 500...

141
00:08:00,400 --> 00:08:02,857
Would you please shut your hole?!

142
00:08:02,940 --> 00:08:04,180
You did it, Okuyasu!

143
00:08:04,420 --> 00:08:05,820
Yeah, but easy, man.

144
00:08:06,020 --> 00:08:08,417
I've had it with your
bullshit, you bastard!

145
00:08:08,500 --> 00:08:11,117
You're giving the run his
7,000 yen back right now!

146
00:08:11,200 --> 00:08:12,030
Are we clear?

147
00:08:26,440 --> 00:08:28,160
My front tooth!

148
00:08:29,820 --> 00:08:30,650
Geez,

149
00:08:30,733 --> 00:08:34,117
why the hell did you stumble around like
a drunk baby and make yourself fall over?

150
00:08:34,200 --> 00:08:35,780
Make myself fall?

151
00:08:35,980 --> 00:08:36,900
You're so mean!

152
00:08:37,400 --> 00:08:40,224
How could you say such a
thing after hitting me?

153
00:08:41,160 --> 00:08:43,572
My poor front tooth has been knocked out.

154
00:08:44,460 --> 00:08:45,290
That's...

155
00:08:45,373 --> 00:08:46,203
that's cruel.

156
00:08:46,286 --> 00:08:47,157
Hey, wait a second.

157
00:08:47,240 --> 00:08:48,416
You are okay, right?

158
00:08:48,560 --> 00:08:51,000
No, stop, Okuyasu. It's a trap.

159
00:08:51,280 --> 00:08:54,339
Whatever you do, don't let
him make you feel guilty.

160
00:08:57,560 --> 00:08:59,220
He guilted you on purpose.

161
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:05,580
A front tooth will cost me a pretty
penny, and I don't have any insurance.

162
00:09:07,420 --> 00:09:09,860
Damn, you little... Uh-oh!

163
00:09:10,120 --> 00:09:11,817
I wouldn't do that if I were you!

164
00:09:11,900 --> 00:09:15,377
If someone under my locks control
tries to hurt me in any way,

165
00:09:15,460 --> 00:09:18,813
the damage will bounce back
and hurt my opponent instead!

166
00:09:19,180 --> 00:09:20,760
Shit, you bastard!

167
00:09:23,380 --> 00:09:26,540
Hey, about that kitten
you said Koichi ran over.

168
00:09:26,780 --> 00:09:28,368
Would this happen to be it?

169
00:09:31,640 --> 00:09:33,120
That's a stuffed animal.

170
00:09:35,100 --> 00:09:36,880
Now, getting down to business.

171
00:09:37,180 --> 00:09:39,004
I've got your tooth right here.

172
00:09:39,780 --> 00:09:41,080
It's as good as new.

173
00:09:47,260 --> 00:09:48,880
It's gone! Yeah, I know!

174
00:09:49,120 --> 00:09:51,414
And I feel a million times lighter now!

175
00:09:51,700 --> 00:09:53,257
Just who the hell are you?

176
00:09:53,340 --> 00:09:56,046
Hey, did you forget about
the 7,000 you stole?

177
00:09:57,480 --> 00:09:58,310
You win!

178
00:09:58,393 --> 00:09:59,320
Here's the money!

179
00:09:59,660 --> 00:10:02,895
Now hit the road before we
kick your smarmy little ass!

180
00:10:07,360 --> 00:10:08,780
Oh, thank goodness.

181
00:10:09,880 --> 00:10:12,757
He took the bills and only
left the corners behind.

182
00:10:12,840 --> 00:10:15,737
He grabbed more than enough bills
to exchange them at the bank.

183
00:10:15,820 --> 00:10:17,120
What a douchebag.

184
00:10:17,980 --> 00:10:20,740
He'll pay, and it's not even my money.

185
00:10:24,560 --> 00:10:26,720
Damn, easily 7,000 yen.

186
00:10:27,900 --> 00:10:30,597
But they haven't gotten
rid of me that easily.

187
00:10:30,680 --> 00:10:31,920
I'll get my revenge.

188
00:10:43,620 --> 00:10:46,738
That rotten morning practically
ruined my entire day.

189
00:10:46,880 --> 00:10:48,140
I'm glad it's over.

190
00:10:48,940 --> 00:10:50,140
I'm home, police.

191
00:10:51,120 --> 00:10:53,880
You didn't die, did you? Woof, woof!

192
00:10:54,260 --> 00:10:55,977
Hey, Mom, I'm home from school.

193
00:10:56,060 --> 00:10:59,577
Truth be told, I've heard
quite a lot about you, ma 'am.

194
00:10:59,660 --> 00:11:02,920
Beautiful, kind, and so refined.

195
00:11:04,400 --> 00:11:05,940
Oh, don't be silly.

196
00:11:06,280 --> 00:11:07,460
No, it's all true.

197
00:11:07,940 --> 00:11:08,937
Are you serious?

198
00:11:09,020 --> 00:11:10,844
Cross my heart and hope to die.

199
00:11:13,100 --> 00:11:14,820
Why is this guy in my house?

200
00:11:14,980 --> 00:11:17,680
And why is he massaging
my mom's shoulders?

201
00:11:25,760 --> 00:11:27,180
Hey, what is this?

202
00:11:27,320 --> 00:11:28,555
And why are you here?

203
00:11:28,880 --> 00:11:29,720
Hi, Ko.

204
00:11:29,940 --> 00:11:31,437
Did you have a good day at school?

205
00:11:31,520 --> 00:11:32,350
Come in.

206
00:11:32,620 --> 00:11:33,973
I asked you a question!

207
00:11:34,140 --> 00:11:35,077
Don't ignore me!

208
00:11:35,160 --> 00:11:37,160
What are you doing here? Koichi,

209
00:11:37,340 --> 00:11:38,977
this gentleman was kind enough to bring us

210
00:11:39,060 --> 00:11:41,648
the money you dropped
on your way to school.

211
00:11:41,740 --> 00:11:42,570
Huh?

212
00:11:42,653 --> 00:11:44,900
7,000 yen, young man. Hold on!

213
00:11:45,040 --> 00:11:46,275
This is unbelievable!

214
00:11:46,580 --> 00:11:47,917
You told her you found it?

215
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:49,040
Well, of course!

216
00:11:49,380 --> 00:11:51,204
After all, you did run into Mr.

217
00:11:51,320 --> 00:11:53,617
Kobayashi on your bike today, didn't you?

218
00:11:53,700 --> 00:11:54,530
What?

219
00:11:54,613 --> 00:11:57,237
I just wanted to make sure you
got your money back, Koichi.

220
00:11:57,320 --> 00:11:59,257
Yeah, it's the least you could do!

221
00:11:59,340 --> 00:12:00,457
I don't understand.

222
00:12:00,540 --> 00:12:02,246
Why are you getting so upset?

223
00:12:02,640 --> 00:12:07,257
There's another thing I should address,
ma 'am, but it's not easy for me to say.

224
00:12:07,340 --> 00:12:10,057
It would seem as though
I too dropped my wallet

225
00:12:10,140 --> 00:12:12,937
when Koichi mowed me down
with his bike this morning.

226
00:12:13,020 --> 00:12:15,600
Funny enough, it looks just like this one.

227
00:12:15,940 --> 00:12:20,058
I figure in all the confusion earlier,
mine was taken in place of his.

228
00:12:20,360 --> 00:12:22,497
Do you understand what
I'm getting at, ma 'am?

229
00:12:22,580 --> 00:12:23,410
Think hard.

230
00:12:23,493 --> 00:12:28,500
Uh, well, that seems like quite the
coincidence, but I suppose it's possible.

231
00:12:28,760 --> 00:12:29,878
Well, there you go.

232
00:12:30,220 --> 00:12:33,985
If you would please tell Koichi
to return my wallet immediately.

233
00:12:34,840 --> 00:12:37,960
It had about 500,000 yen, give or take.

234
00:12:38,180 --> 00:12:40,557
And I would like to be paid back in full.

235
00:12:40,640 --> 00:12:42,297
Oh, good heavens! How much?

236
00:12:42,380 --> 00:12:43,960
500,000?!

237
00:12:44,540 --> 00:12:47,060
I get your game now, dirty con artist!

238
00:12:47,320 --> 00:12:48,380
Ko, what happened?

239
00:12:48,740 --> 00:12:50,297
You don't have to worry, Mom.

240
00:12:50,380 --> 00:12:51,797
This guy is nothing but a fraud.

241
00:12:51,880 --> 00:12:53,600
My, that's so rude!

242
00:12:53,840 --> 00:12:54,877
I didn't want to bring it up,

243
00:12:54,960 --> 00:12:58,580
but I have proof that your
son swiped my wallet for his.

244
00:12:58,840 --> 00:13:02,857
I decided to eat at Johnny's last night,
where I ordered the hamburger meal.

245
00:13:02,940 --> 00:13:04,234
And, oh, that's right!

246
00:13:04,320 --> 00:13:07,260
I had a bowl of onion
Guardian soup on the side.

247
00:13:07,640 --> 00:13:11,920
I believe it came out to 1,833
yen, but I could be wrong.

248
00:13:12,140 --> 00:13:15,905
The receipt in the wallet Koichi
has should clear everything up.

249
00:13:27,180 --> 00:13:29,820
He was telling the truth! No, he's not!

250
00:13:30,100 --> 00:13:31,417
You have to believe me!

251
00:13:31,500 --> 00:13:32,877
It's some kind of trick!

252
00:13:32,960 --> 00:13:34,257
You planned it, didn't you?

253
00:13:34,340 --> 00:13:37,697
Then you went out and bought
the same wallet to trick my mom!

254
00:13:37,780 --> 00:13:39,560
He has quite the imagination,

255
00:13:40,020 --> 00:13:43,961
but his habit of lying and stealing
is a disturbing character flaw.

256
